content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal condition: approximately one drop per second is reported. No numerical allowable seal-leak rate is provided, so that reading cannot be compared with a numeric limit. The applicable manual troubleshooting entry is leakage at the shaft seal; it directs replacement of the mechanical seal and an alignment check. The active drip is therefore actionable even though vibration and temperature do not require an immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable manufacturer scale is Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. Numerically, 3.4 mm/s is in Zone B, 2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled long-term operation. It is above the Zone A boundary of 2.8, below Zone C at 4.5 to 7.1, and not in highest-severity Zone D at 7.1 to 11.0, where the figure says damage is likely and to stop the pump. Confirm that the reported reading is RMS and was taken on a bearing housing before finalising the classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface. The applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 70 C is exactly at the upper normal limit, not above the 80 C alarm limit. SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift only when temperature is above the manufacturer alarm limit, so that P1 trigger does not currently apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate protective actions are not presently triggered: the reported vibration is numerically in Zone B rather than the manufacturer's highest zone, and housing temperature is not above the alarm limit. Seal replacement can proceed as planned maintenance with the pump isolated for the work rather than as an emergency vibration or temperature shutdown.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a leading cause of the shaft-seal leakage. Early failure of component seal HF3-450 is also a leading possibility if that seal is installed: SB-2026-014 attributes such failures on pumps from serial HF3-22000 to a revised sleeve tolerance, and P-104's serial HF3-22871 is within that range. Confirm the installed seal type during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another documented cause of leakage at the shaft seal and requires an alignment check. The 3.4 mm/s reading alone does not establish misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry, which the manual also lists as a possible cause of shaft-seal leakage. This pump has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; no dry-running event is established by the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration or related symptoms persist, secondary causes to investigate are bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, cavitation and misalignment; NPSH should be checked for cavitation. Current Zone B vibration and 70 C housing temperature do not by themselves establish bearing wear or justify bearing replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-104 is on the chemically dosed filtered-water line. Arrange a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment for the back pull-out work.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Using the planned lifting equipment, remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, then remove the impeller nut and impeller in accordance with the mechanical-seal replacement procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve and record the installed seal type. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and determine scoring depth: replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed to set the replacement seal; the scoring inspection is still required to decide whether the sleeve itself must be replaced.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is accessible, inspect the bearings and impeller and record any wear, noise or damage. Check NPSH if cavitation is suspected or vibration remains unexplained. Do not replace bearings solely because of the current readings; if bearing wear, noise or high temperature is confirmed, replace drive-end and non-drive-end bearings as a pair under a revised scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new pre-set cartridge mechanical seal HF3-450B and one new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm as required by SB-2026-014; do not use the superseded 25 Nm value for this seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble the pump and tighten applicable Table 5 fasteners, whose torques are specified for lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm where disturbed. The seal-gland requirement for the installed HF3-450B remains 30 Nm under the service bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as part of the shaft-seal leakage corrective action. Use laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm; record the measured results.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before running, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry. During recommissioning, record seal leakage, vibration and housing temperature. If vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If housing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift; the manual trip value is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one; mandatory replacement type for this serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450. No sleeve setting measurement is needed, and seal gland nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity one; fit a new gasket during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, quantity one conditional on inspection: replace only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Confirm the actual scoring depth during disassembly before using this part.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, SSP-07 requires electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and therefore exceeds the SSP-07 threshold of 25 kg. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment; the manual also states that lifting equipment is required for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Pumps P-101 through P-106 on the filtered-water line are dosed with sodium hypochlorite. For this chemically dosed line, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional SSP-07 responses for recommissioning: vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart; bearing temperature above the manufacturer alarm limit requires a P1 work order within the shift. The present 3.4 mm/s Zone B value and 70 C temperature do not trigger either response.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard labour allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance is 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Laser alignment is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing; an alignment check is also specified for shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing work only: replacement of the bearing pair has a standard allowance of 6.0 hours with 2 technicians. Do not add this to the base scope unless inspection or operation establishes wear, noise or high temperature requiring pair replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the Revision D manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and to use HF3-450B instead. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, so the bulletin's explicit serial range applies and HF3-450B is selected. The manual route for pumps below HF3-22000 does not apply to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because this asset is in the bulletin serial range and will receive HF3-450B, use 30 Nm. The previous-shift note claiming that 25 Nm is correct for all pumps is rejected for this work order; it does not override the asset-specific bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 3.4 mm/s vibration measured as RMS velocity on a bearing housing, as required by the Figure 3 severity scale? The fault report does not state the measurement basis or exact measurement location (C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and does shaft sleeve HF3-455 have scoring deeper than 0.1 mm? The installed seal type affects the failure history, and the scoring depth determines whether the conditional sleeve is required; neither changes the requirement to use HF3-450B for this serial range (C13).",
    "Was Plan 11 flush continuously available, and is there any history of dry running? This would help distinguish dry-run damage from seal-face wear or bulletin-related early failure (C02, C09).",
    "What are the actual alignment, bearing, impeller and NPSH findings? The supplied readings do not diagnose these conditions. If bearing-pair replacement is justified, revise the scope to include HF3-512 and HF3-510 and the associated conditional labour (C05, C09, C10, C12).",
    "The evidence provides no numerical acceptable seal-drip rate for final acceptance and no site P1/P2/P3 priority matrix or required completion date. The leak is treated under the manual's shaft-seal leakage troubleshooting action; P2 is a planning judgement because active leakage needs repair while the documented immediate-stop and P1 temperature triggers are not met (C09, C07, C02, C15)."
  ]
}
